WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:05.560
Cursing at children? Flashing a co-star?&nbsp;
Actor Tim Allen may play Santa Claus,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.560 --> 00:00:09.240
but co-star Casey Wilson&nbsp;
says he's anything but jolly.

00:00:09.240 --> 00:00:13.640
Casey Wilson acted alongside Tim Allen in&nbsp;
the pilot episode of The Santa Clauses,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.640 --> 00:00:17.360
a Disney+ series that serves as a&nbsp;
sequel to Allen's three The Santa&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.360 --> 00:00:21.800
Clause movies. On the podcast B---h&nbsp;
Sesh, Wilson described Allen as, quote,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.800 --> 00:00:26.640
"so f---ing rude." She discussed filming a scene&nbsp;
with the star where Santa comes down a chimney,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:30.280
and Wilson's character proceeds to&nbsp;
throw things at him. She explained,

00:00:30.280 --> 00:00:33.800
"He goes over to the producer who is&nbsp;
standing four feet from me and goes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:38.520
and I hear him, he goes, 'You gotta tell her&nbsp;
to stop stepping on my lines.' The producer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:42.927
turns to me with horror on his face and&nbsp;
has to walk one foot to me and he goes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.927 --> 00:00:45.767
'Um, Tim would ask that you&nbsp;
stop stepping on his lines.'"

00:00:45.880 --> 00:00:50.160
As if that wasn't enough, Wilson said that at&nbsp;
the end of a scene, Allen loudly proclaimed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:55.200
that he was leaving and dropped his cape onto&nbsp;
the floor for others to pick up. She concluded,

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:59.440
"He's a b---h. [...] I will not say who said&nbsp;
this. This was someone that I do not know,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.440 --> 00:01:04.720
perhaps in the crew. [He or she] breezes past me&nbsp;
and just goes, 'You're seeing him on a good day.'"

00:01:04.720 --> 00:01:08.960
As of this video, Allen has yet to respond&nbsp;
to Wilson's remarks. But it would be in line&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.960 --> 00:01:13.184
with other behind-the-scenes stories that have&nbsp;
come out regarding the actor over the years.

00:01:13.184 --> 00:01:16.920
For a show about Santa Claus that airs&nbsp;
on Disney+, The Santa Clauses seems to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.920 --> 00:01:21.880
find itself mired in controversy constantly.&nbsp;
Viewers were annoyed by one joke in particular&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.880 --> 00:01:26.683
in Season 1, which was clearly inspired&nbsp;
by a popular conservative talking point.

00:01:26.683 --> 00:01:30.363
"Saying 'Merry Christmas to all'&nbsp;
has suddenly become problematic."

00:01:30.363 --> 00:01:33.840
Now, Allen is once again in the hot&nbsp;
seat, and it's his alleged behavior&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.840 --> 00:01:36.080
while filming that's put him in the line of fire.

00:01:36.080 --> 00:01:40.720
It shouldn't exactly be news that Allen&nbsp;
has a short fuse. In a 2021 interview on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.720 --> 00:01:44.800
The Kelly Clarkson Show, Allen spoke about&nbsp;
an incident on the set of The Santa Clause&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.800 --> 00:01:49.360
2 where they were shooting a scene involving a&nbsp;
bunch of children. A couple of the kids began&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.360 --> 00:01:53.040
acting up and preventing them from getting&nbsp;
the shot they needed. As Allen put it,

00:01:53.040 --> 00:01:57.200
"The kid said one more word, and I let out&nbsp;
the loudest F-bomb. And I turned around,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.200 --> 00:02:00.840
and there are 12 children — it looked&nbsp;
like you had ripped their legs off."

00:02:00.840 --> 00:02:04.520
"Their Santa has just screamed the F-bomb."

00:02:04.520 --> 00:02:09.040
He added that he recognized his mistake, and&nbsp;
even though Disney tried to do damage control,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.040 --> 00:02:13.000
what was done was done. But Allen's&nbsp;
unprofessional behavior allegedly goes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:16.720
back much further — to his Home&nbsp;
Improvement days in the 1990s.

00:02:16.720 --> 00:02:21.280
Pamela Anderson wrote about Allen in her memoir,&nbsp;
Love, Pamela, recalling an incident on the set&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.280 --> 00:02:25.960
of Home Improvement where he allegedly&nbsp;
flashed his genitalia at her. Variety&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.960 --> 00:02:30.080
published an excerpt about the incident&nbsp;
from the book, in which Anderson wrote,

00:02:30.080 --> 00:02:35.160
"He opened his robe and flashed me quickly —&nbsp;
completely naked underneath. He said it was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.160 --> 00:02:39.880
only fair, because he had seen me naked.&nbsp;
Now we're even. I laughed uncomfortably."

00:02:39.880 --> 00:02:42.720
Allen denied the incident&nbsp;
in a statement to Variety.

00:02:42.720 --> 00:02:47.000
These accusations may explain why Hollywood&nbsp;
doesn't really cast Allen anymore, outside&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:52.440
of his main franchises like The Santa Clause. With&nbsp;
Season 2 of the Disney+ series wrapped, and seeing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.440 --> 00:02:57.320
how it hasn't been renewed for Season 3 quite&nbsp;
yet, it's possible that Casey Wilson's story,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.320 --> 00:03:02.760
as well as others concerning Allen, could convince&nbsp;
Disney to drop the show like a hot piece of coal.

00:03:02.760 --> 00:03:04.773
"Merry Christmas, Sarah."

